    "problems": "The experiments do not sweep model size, token count, or compute and do not measure held-out cross-entropy, so they cannot establish a power law or test compute-optimal allocations. The first controlled comparison uses one approximately 3B-parameter model; uncertainty estimates are not reported. The knowledge-density measure is an approximate LLM-assisted proxy.",
    "rows_left_out": "Individual benchmark scores from Tables 3–10 are not listed separately; the rows record the reported aggregate category averages instead. The paper reports many separate benchmark values, but they are not measurements of any claim version's named outcome and the aggregate results capture the relevant training-configuration comparisons.",
